title: Aegis APPROVE voice capture A1/A2; the kernel trusts the client's account of how a turn ended (M1)
summary: |-
  Aegis approved 6ca8f0a3, f06ac152 and f55af625:
  - the voice principal only;
  - closed enums;
  - a 5 s TTL;
  - visibility limited to human and voice (gui-only text seam);
  - no words on drops;
  - the L1 and L2 fixes verified;
  - the 175 ms poll is fine.
  A compromised voice client cannot inject text into the GUI, but it can mislead state: keep "hearing" lit, fake "Got it", or report dropped/refused for a turn that was actually delivered. That is M1: the kernel should cross-check terminal states against its own send/append outcome. L1: the text seam should also check the class. L2: GUI-side staleness on failed reads. L3: the capture slot is not keyed to connId. L4: the client report queue is unbounded if the kernel hangs. All five were sent to the builder before merge.
symbols_touched:
  - '#gnomon-voice'
  - '#gui-voice-capture'
learnings:
  - Status relayed from a semi-trusted client should be cross-checked against what the kernel itself observed whenever the kernel has ground truth (send accepted or refused).
verification:
  status: pass
  details:
    verdict: APPROVE
